soc: cix: expose audited bus performance domains through devfreq

Replace the removed CIX/Sky1 engineering interface with a standard devfreq
consumer for the CI-700 and multimedia-fabric SCMI performance domains.
Enumerate and validate every firmware-provided OPP, including its nonzero,
strictly increasing frequency and SCMI level, then publish the same
frequency table on each CIX bus device.

The default userspace governor makes no performance-state request until an
administrator selects a frequency.  Standard performance and powersave
governors can select the validated maximum and minimum when configured.
The first control request captures the provider's current state and holds a
balanced runtime-PM reference; driver removal restores that state before
detaching.  Firmware may acknowledge a request before readback reflects the
new state, so transitions and restoration use bounded polling and never
publish the preceding frequency as the completed result.

No automatic load governor is selected.  Neither domain currently exposes a
qualified busy/total-time signal, so inventing utilization from CPU load or
unrelated PMU events would not be a sound basis for bus policy.

The device identities and domain intent trace to
Sky1-Linux/linux-sky1@57e018a398248d7e5e4d798610df79a557c0629f;
the reduced devfreq implementation is overlay-created.  Retained patch 0008
provides the exported ACPI named-domain attachment and module lifetime
ownership, while 30200 provides SCMI provider-state readback.

diff --git a/drivers/soc/cix/Kconfig b/drivers/soc/cix/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/soc/cix/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/cix/Kconfig
@@ -33,3 +33,23 @@ config CIX_ACPI_USB_SCAN
 	  the overlapping vendor USB devices. With firmware that exposes only
 	  one model, the helper either stands down or allows the vendor-only
 	  devices to enumerate unchanged.
+
+config CIX_BUS_PERF
+	tristate "CIX Sky1 bus performance domains"
+	depends on ARCH_CIX || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on OF || ACPI
+	depends on PM_DEVFREQ
+	depends on ARM_SCMI_PERF_DOMAIN
+	select PM_OPP
+	select DEVFREQ_GOV_USERSPACE
+	default ARCH_CIX
+	help
+	  Enable support for the CI-700 and multimedia-fabric SCMI
+	  performance domains on CIX Sky1 systems. The driver validates the
+	  firmware-provided OPPs and exposes them through devfreq. The
+	  userspace governor preserves the firmware-selected state until a
+	  policy request is made; performance and powersave governors may
+	  also be selected when they are available. It uses only standard
+	  devfreq controls and does not expose mutable engineering controls.
+
+	  ACPI firmware exposes these consumers as CIXHA030 and CIXHA031.
